The likely culprit is that even when the IAM role grants S3 GetObject/ListBucket, Amazon Personalize also requires the S3 bucket policy itself to explicitly allow the "personalize.amazonaws.com" service principal, and if the bucket uses SSE-KMS encryption the KMS key policy needs to grant decrypt access too. I want to verify this bucket-policy requirement against AWS documentation before stating it as fact.

"}]}

